 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "African cities grow very fast, mainly because of rural exodus and high birth rates. Problems:\n• housing shortage and shanty towns; high rents;\n• unemployment and underemployment; poverty;\n• traffic jams, poor roads, accidents;\n• insufficient water, electricity and health services; load shedding (power cuts);\n• waste and pollution: rubbish heaps, blocked gutters, floods, air pollution from vehicles and factories;\n• insecurity: theft, aggression, drug abuse;\n• diseases: cholera, malaria, typhoid.\nSolutions: town planning, low-cost housing, better public transport, waste collection (HYSACAM), new jobs, family planning, developing rural areas to reduce exodus.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {},
  "problem": "Why are floods common in some quarters of Douala and Yaoundé?",
  "steps": [
   "Rubbish is thrown into gutters and streams, blocking them.",
   "Houses are built in swampy areas, so heavy rain cannot drain away."
  ],
  "answer": "Blocked gutters and building in swampy areas.",
  "checks": []
 },
